WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.412 --> 00:00:03.479
Unit four. Personal Boundaries and Respect!

2
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:07.949
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.999 --> 00:00:10.921
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.971 --> 00:00:14.952
Today we learn about Personal Boundaries and Respect. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:19.189
Boundary. Say it with me. Boundary!

6
00:00:22.657 --> 00:00:25.991
Consent. Say it with me. Consent!

7
00:00:29.554 --> 00:00:32.837
Respect. Say it with me. Respect!

8
00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:39.835
Comfort level. Say it with me. Comfort level!

9
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.063
Communication. Say it with me. Communication!

10
00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:54.558
Personal space. Say it with me. Personal space!

11
00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:01.589
Assertive. Say it with me. Assertive!

12
00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:08.350
Mutual. Say it with me. Mutual!

13
00:01:11.889 --> 00:01:23.687
Understanding my own boundary and comfort level is an important life skill. Respect means asking for consent and listening when someone communicates their personal space. Mutual, assertive communication builds trust.

14
00:01:23.737 --> 00:01:26.579
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:28.233 --> 00:01:33.257
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:33.307 --> 00:01:34.457
Respect!

17
00:01:35.348 --> 00:01:40.411
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:40.461 --> 00:01:41.611
Assertive!

19
00:01:42.496 --> 00:01:48.854
Did you know? Clearly communicating your own boundaries actually helps others trust and respect you more.

20
00:01:48.904 --> 00:01:50.800
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:51.519 --> 00:01:59.751
Think and answer. Why is it important to respect other people's boundaries?

22
00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:00.951
Great answer!

23
00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:06.373
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:06.423 --> 00:02:08.828
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

